WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.352
The farmer who

00:00:01.164 --> 00:00:02.956
photographed five thousand

00:00:02.767 --> 00:00:03.675
snowflakes

00:00:04.206 --> 00:00:05.680
In 1885

00:00:05.786 --> 00:00:06.953
Vermont farm boy

00:00:06.765 --> 00:00:08.144
Wilson Bentley bolted

00:00:07.956 --> 00:00:08.769
a camera to

00:00:08.581 --> 00:00:09.937
his mother's microscope

00:00:09.949 --> 00:00:10.680
and caught the

00:00:10.491 --> 00:00:11.871
first photograph of

00:00:11.682 --> 00:00:12.814
a snow crystal

00:00:13.342 --> 00:00:14.167
He spent the

00:00:13.979 --> 00:00:15.441
next forty-six winters

00:00:15.252 --> 00:00:16.231
doing it again

00:00:16.455 --> 00:00:17.634
photographing more

00:00:17.446 --> 00:00:18.613
than five thousand

00:00:18.425 --> 00:00:19.250
crystals

00:00:19.389 --> 00:00:20.426
Every one had

00:00:20.238 --> 00:00:21.605
six-fold symmetry

00:00:22.142 --> 00:00:24.040
In November 1931

00:00:24.288 --> 00:00:25.538
McGraw-Hill published

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:26.434
Snow Crystals

00:00:26.517 --> 00:00:27.354
with more than

00:00:27.166 --> 00:00:29.052
2,400 of his

00:00:28.864 --> 00:00:29.830
photographs

00:00:29.969 --> 00:00:30.995
His father had

00:00:30.807 --> 00:00:31.773
thought the camera

00:00:31.585 --> 00:00:32.245
a waste of

00:00:32.057 --> 00:00:32.634
money

00:00:32.658 --> 00:00:33.389
and bought it

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:33.896
anyway

00:00:34.422 --> 00:00:35.436
Full story on

00:00:35.247 --> 00:00:36.143
the dashboard
